{{~##
Open Graph Image Partial - Lumina Theme

Emits og:image (+ width/height) for a social preview of one image. Social crawlers
need an absolute URL and handle JPEG best, and the original file is often far too
large, so this picks a generated variant: the largest size up to 1920px, else the
smallest available size; JPEG when the site generates it. Photos published in
Display P3 (og_image.gamut == 'p3') use their untagged sRGB JPEG ('srgb.jpg',
written at that same size), because social platforms often drop colour profiles.

Expects:
- og_image: Image { slug, width, height, sizes, gamut } (nothing is emitted when null)
- image_formats: Array of generated formats ["avif", "webp", "jpg"]
- base_url: Absolute site URL (nothing is emitted without it)
##~}}
{{~ if !base_url || !og_image || !og_image.sizes || og_image.sizes.size == 0; ret; end ~}}
{{~ include 'imagehelpers' ~}}
{{~ og_size = image_size og_image 1920 ~}}
{{~ og_format = image_fallback_format ~}}
{{~ for format in image_formats; if format == 'jpg'; og_format = 'jpg'; end; end ~}}
{{~ if og_image.gamut == 'p3'; og_format = 'srgb.jpg'; end ~}}
{{~ # Sizes describe the longest edge (resizeMode "longest"); the short edge is rounded. ~}}
{{~ if og_image.width >= og_image.height ~}}
{{~ og_width = og_size; og_height = (2 * og_size * og_image.height + og_image.width) // (2 * og_image.width) ~}}
{{~ else ~}}
{{~ og_height = og_size; og_width = (2 * og_size * og_image.width + og_image.height) // (2 * og_image.height) ~}}
{{~ end ~}}
<meta property="og:image" content="{{ html_escape (absolute_variant_url og_image og_size og_format) }}">
<meta property="og:image:width" content="{{ html_escape og_width }}">
<meta property="og:image:height" content="{{ html_escape og_height }}">
